# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.storeapps: a real store front-end on the full-driver image.
#
# TrollApps (TheResonanceTeam/TrollApps 2.3, org.resonance.store) is the app-store alternative
# built on TrollStore: it lists AltStore-style JSON repositories, downloads the IPA and hands it
# to TrollStore through apple-magnifier://, which the TrollStore.app in /Applications already
# declares (its Info.plist carries the scheme).  The scene joins Wi-Fi first, sets TrollStore up
# the proven way (helper + its own MCM container with ldid), installs TrollApps with the helper,
# and opens it.
#
# The store's source list is pre-seeded instead of added through trollapps://add: TrollApps keeps
# it in UserDefaults under "repos" (a JSON array in a string, see userland/trollstore/
# org.resonance.store.plist), so the app's first fetch already has the LAN source.  Its bundled
# GitHub sources stalled for 60 s in the 02:09 run; the LAN source answers in milliseconds and
# makes the row the GET tap must hit predictable.  The app's own language is set to zh-hans in
# the same file, so the store draws its Chinese UI without touching the system language.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 20 joinfile /redwood/fw/network
/redwood/bin/net_test show dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 25 store wait 20
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 25
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/bin/hk-appinstall.sh TrollStore.app com.opa334.TrollStore
/redwood/bin/mcm_test com.opa334.TrollStore /Applications/TrollStore.app /redwood/share/tsldid/ldid
/var/jb/usr/bin/mkdir -p /var/mobile/Library/Preferences
/var/jb/usr/bin/cp /redwood/share/trollstore/com.opa334.TrollStore.plist /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/
/var/jb/usr/bin/chown 501:501 /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/com.opa334.TrollStore.plist
/var/jb/usr/bin/chmod 644 /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/com.opa334.TrollStore.plist
/var/jb/usr/bin/cp /redwood/share/trollstore/org.resonance.store.plist /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/
/var/jb/usr/bin/chown 501:501 /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/org.resonance.store.plist
/var/jb/usr/bin/chmod 644 /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/org.resonance.store.plist
# The persona spawn the store app itself depends on, measured on its own first: the program
# drops to 501 and asks posix_spawn for persona 99 with uid/gid 0 (TrollApps' spawnRoot), then
# repeats the spawn without the persona as the control.  Its lines in the run log say whether
# the helper spawn can work before the UI gets a chance to try it.
/redwood/bin/persona_spawn_test
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
/redwood/bin/persona_spawn_test uid501
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
# The IPA is not in the payload: the root image beside the kernel tops out near 50 MB (the
# 5.5 MB IPA made the upload fail).  hk_download fetches it from the machine on the LAN that
# serves it, which also proves the phone can download bytes over the Wi-Fi this scene joined.
/redwood/bin/hk_download http://192.168.0.104:8000/TrollApps.ipa /private/var/tmp/TrollApps.ipa
/var/jb/usr/bin/chmod 644 /private/var/tmp/TrollApps.ipa
/var/jb/Applications/TrollStore.app/trollstorehelper install custom /private/var/tmp/TrollApps.ipa
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20
/var/jb/usr/bin/uicache -a
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen --bundleid org.resonance.store
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 15
# The first launch shows the "What's New in 2.3" sheet; Next takes it to the catalog.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.91
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 10
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.91
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 15
# Featured: the one source is the LAN one, so LocProbe's row is the first row and its GET sits
# at the same place the first row's button did in the 02:43 screenshot (0.86, 0.273).
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.86 0.273
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 15
# GET leaves the queue sheet collapsed at 105 pt; its bottom 83 pt are hidden by the tab bar
# (the 03:35 run's swipe started there and the sheet never moved).  The drag indicator at
# 0.885 is a Button in BottomSheet (BottomSheetView+DragIndicatorAction.swift): a tap switches
# to the next position, .relativeTop(0.975), full height.  A slow drag from the same point is
# the fallback, and is harmless once the sheet is up.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.885
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 5
/redwood/bin/rwtouch drag 0.5 0.885 0.5 0.25 600 400
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 5
# Confirm is the blue button above Clear Queue: with the sheet's 95 pt bottom padding (canClose
# is true until Confirm) it spans 0.740..0.804 of the screen, centre 0.772; the three taps are
# inside that span and stay above Clear Queue (0.814..0.878).  Once one lands, canClose turns
# false and the buttons move down 55 pt, so the later taps hit the list, not Clear Queue.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.75
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.78
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.76
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30
# With skip_install_prompt the app downloads and then spawns TrollStore's helper itself; the
# queue file is removed by the app after the helper returns.  The container list says whether
# the helper installed; then the app it installed is started to show that it runs.
/var/jb/usr/bin/ls -la /var/mobile/.TrollApps/tmp/ >> /private/var/tmp/storeapps.txt
/var/jb/usr/bin/ls -l /var/containers/Bundle/Application >> /private/var/tmp/storeapps.txt
/var/jb/usr/bin/uicache -a
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen --bundleid com.hakios.locprobe
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20
/var/jb/usr/bin/ls -l /var/containers/Bundle/Application >> /private/var/tmp/storeapps.txt
/var/jb/usr/bin/cat /private/var/tmp/storeapps.txt
